{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "truenas",
  "description": "The full seven-request walk of a TrueNAS SCALE system: system/info, network/configuration, interface, pool, disk, app, and vm. Proves the NAS becomes one asset carrying its own interfaces, its chassis identity, its pool and disk inventory, and its applications as software plus published ports as services -- and that virtual machines become their own assets keyed on the middleware row id. Three VM cases are covered: one with a virtual NIC, whose MAC is read from the device list embedded on the VM row so the separate /vm/device endpoint is never requested; one with no NIC at all but a DNS-shaped name, which is imported on the name alone; and one whose name is free text an operator typed, which has no MAC and no usable name and must be skipped rather than have 'Windows 11 Desktop' imported as a hostname and correlate two unrelated guests. The lo and docker0 interfaces must be filtered as guest and container plumbing. Payload shapes are taken from the TrueNAS middleware's own API models: system.info from plugins/system/info.py, InterfaceEntry/InterfaceEntryState from api/v25_10_0/interface.py, NetworkConfigurationEntry from api/v25_10_2/network_configuration.py, PoolEntry and DiskEntry from api/v25_10_2/{pool,disk}.py, AppEntry/AppActiveWorkloads/UsedPorts/HostPorts from api/v25_04_0/app.py, and VMEntry/VMStatus/VMDeviceEntry/VMNICDevice from api/v25_04_2/{vm,vm_device}.py. All data is synthetic.",
